# Release configuration, in one file instead of spread across a keychain, a doc table and
# two scripts' defaults. Copy to `.env` and fill in; `.env` is gitignored and never leaves
# this machine.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `scripts/release-sign.sh` reads it, and `scripts/release.sh` reaches it through that.
# Anything already exported in the environment wins, so a one-off override still works:
#
#     SIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Someone Else (TEAMID)" ./scripts/release.sh
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT IN HERE: the notarization password. `NOTARY_PROFILE` names a
# keychain profile that already holds the Apple ID and its app-specific password, encrypted
# by macOS and unreadable as plaintext. Putting that password in a dotfile would move a
# real secret out of the keychain and into a file that backups, editors and greps can see,
# which is a downgrade — so this file names the profile and lets the keychain keep the
# secret. Create the profile once:
#
#     xcrun notarytool store-credentials tenon-notary \
#       --apple-id "$NOTARY_APPLE_ID" --team-id "$NOTARY_TEAM_ID" \
#       --password <app-specific-password>
#
# App-specific passwords come from appleid.apple.com → Sign-In and Security. They cannot be
# read back afterwards, from the keychain or anywhere else — a lost one is replaced, not
# recovered.

# The identity codesign signs a distributed build with. Must be a Developer ID Application
# certificate: an Apple Development certificate signs nothing that another machine will run.
# Leave empty to let release-sign.sh discover it, which is safe only while exactly one
# Developer ID identity is in the keychain — it refuses to guess between two.
SIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Your Company (TEAMID)"

# The notarytool keychain profile created by the command above.
NOTARY_PROFILE="tenon-notary"

# Team ID. Needed to recreate the profile, and as the value of the MACOS/NOTARY team
# secrets if the release workflow is ever given credentials.
NOTARY_TEAM_ID="TEAMID"

# The Apple ID the profile was created with. Not used when the profile already exists;
# recorded so recreating it does not require remembering which account signed up.
NOTARY_APPLE_ID=""
